# game: this repository

# the project's name, and nothing about anyone's disk. the two remotes
# it maps to -- the road that takes every commit, and the dist that only
# game release pushes to -- live in the builder's own config, so a
# checkout carries no path that is true on one machine.
name puffin-dist

# the lint is the dotfile's, whole. a repository that describes any lint
# describes all of it, so describing none here takes width, rows,
# comments, print, exclaim, shout and the word list as they stand. what
# the tree still owes against that list is paid before the release, not
# excused in this file.

# install puts the binary where a user-scoped binary belongs, stamped with
# the commit's subject, which go does not record on its own. PREFIX and
# TAGS are read from the environment by the script.
target install . :: sh tools/install

# formula renders the homebrew formula for a released tag, so the tap and
# the release cannot drift apart. VERSION names the tag.
target formula . :: sh tools/formula
